// TAGEX — O&M Site Visit Scheduler + Tickets, ported into the operations platform.
//
// Was a standalone page (tagex-merged-om-scheduler/index.html, 1,916 lines) in which every
// user pasted an Airtable Personal Access Token, kept in localStorage as `tagex_pat`, and
// identified themselves through a JavaScript prompt() stored as `tagex_user`.
//
// WHAT CHANGED
//   - The PAT is gone. All seven Airtable calls go through TX.api -> /api/at.
//   - Identity is the signed-in session, not a typed-in name.
//   - The token gate is gone; the platform's login screen covers this module.
//   - Inline on*= handlers are gone, so the Content-Security-Policy can stay strict.
//   - Its CSS is scoped to .mod-scheduler (public/css/scheduler.css) so the two apps
//     cannot restyle one another.
//
// WHAT DID NOT CHANGE
//   The calendar, dashboard, tickets and all their behaviour. Beyond the API shim at the
//   top and the wiring at the bottom, this is the original logic.

